# Shared surface pieces. See ../../common/qmldir for why this file must exist.
Strut 1.0 Strut.qml
Pill 1.0 Pill.qml
Icon 1.0 Icon.qml
# The three notch status symbols only, in Microsoft's open Fluent set. A type of
# its own rather than a family property on Icon, so tests/icons.sh can tell the
# two fonts apart — a second family behind the same component would walk past
# the glyph check entirely.
FluentIcon 1.0 FluentIcon.qml
BarText 1.0 BarText.qml
LevelRow 1.0 LevelRow.qml
LocationPicker 1.0 LocationPicker.qml
GlassPane 1.0 GlassPane.qml
AppIcon 1.0 AppIcon.qml
SignalBars 1.0 SignalBars.qml
# A wired connection, drawn for the same reason SignalBars is: Material Icons
# Round has no ethernet glyph anybody recognises. See the file for the measured
# list of names that are not in it.
WiredIcon 1.0 WiredIcon.qml
# The network symbol — wired, four wifi grades, off — in ONE place, because the
# island and the quick panel's tile were drawing two different answers to the
# same question. Reported as "das wifi icon ist voll komisch".
NetIcon 1.0 NetIcon.qml
IconRail 1.0 IconRail.qml
# The two-stage lock/greeter face: clock alone, then clock lifted with identity
# underneath. ONE component for both screens on his instruction — the screen
# before logging in and the one after locking must not look like two products.
StagedFace 1.0 StagedFace.qml
# ⚠️ A SIBLING of the Flickable it reports on, never a child — a child lands in
# the contentItem and scrolls away instead of indicating. The file spells out
# the arithmetic; it shipped the wrong way round in the settings window.
ScrollIndicator 1.0 ScrollIndicator.qml
Tooltip 1.0 Tooltip.qml
Toggle 1.0 Toggle.qml
TextField 1.0 TextField.qml
# Which popup list is open, so the WINDOW can close it on the next press. A
# popup is its own Wayland surface and cannot see the click beside it — measured
# in tools/popup-close-check.qml, after three attempts to detect it from inside.
singleton OpenMenu 1.0 OpenMenu.qml
Dropdown 1.0 Dropdown.qml
# The open counterpart of Dropdown: a typeable field whose suggestions live
# behind a ▾ instead of in a Flow of pills. Dropdown is for a CLOSED list of
# four or more; this is for `pick`, `picks` and `command`, where a value the
# machine has never seen is still legal.
SuggestField 1.0 SuggestField.qml
# Choose a directory without GTK — A4. Qt.labs.folderlistmodel does the reading,
# so there is no process per navigation step; the package is already quickshell's
# own runtime.
FolderPicker 1.0 FolderPicker.qml
# A colour of your own, for the one row where a list of prepared swatches would
# be the same closed set the palettes already are.
ColourPicker 1.0 ColourPicker.qml
# The password field of the lock screen and the greeter — ONE component, because
# B24 says they are one face. It was built twice, near enough identically that
# the two would have drifted the first time either was adjusted. Transparent and
# smaller than a normal pill (his request), and it knows how to shake, which is
# what a wrong password does instead of printing a sentence.
PasswordField 1.0 PasswordField.qml

# ⚠️ ONE PICKER, TWO USERS — themes and wallpapers. He sent the second
# screenshot with the words "genau so für wallpaper switcher", which is the
# brief: the SAME component with different tiles, not a second one that looks
# similar. The tile is a Component handed in; this file knows about a row, a
# size, a ring and a counter and nothing about palettes or pictures.
CarouselPicker 1.0 CarouselPicker.qml
